{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record is data the linker places in a section, so nothing runs for it at launch. Reading a set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"walks every loaded image’s section once and calls the accessor of each record of the set’s kind.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"That’s linear in the records the program holds, and the reads aren’t cached, so read a set once","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"where the program starts and keep the array. ","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSetsPerformanceTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" checks the scaling in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"release builds: reading 3,000 records costs no more than about 10 times reading 300.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The build pays for each marked declaration: the macro’s expansion and the record it compiles to."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"That cost is also linear while the records are spread across files, as they are in an app."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thousands of records in one file take the compiler much longer, so generated registries are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"better split."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Measured","anchor":"Measured"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"just benchmark"},{"type":"text","text":" measures both in a SwiftPM package of generated records, against the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declarations without the macro. These figures are from an M1 Ultra with Swift 6.4.2, in a debug"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"build, with each size’s records split across 10 files:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"alignments":["right","right","right","right"],"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Records"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Build time the records add"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Per record"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading every record (release)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"100"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2.6 s"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"26 ms","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"77 µs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1,000"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.2 s"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.3 ms"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"242 µs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"10,000","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"50 s"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"5.0 ms","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2.0 ms","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The 100-record row is mostly the macro plugin’s start-up, paid once per module that uses it. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read also has a fixed part, the walk over every image the process has loaded, which is about"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"70 µs on macOS. In a single file, 10,000 records added 111 s to the build instead of 50 s."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking"],"anchor":"Guides","generated":true}],"abstract":[{"text":"What records cost as an app grows: nothing at launch, a walk of the records when a set is read,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a few milliseconds of build time per marked declaration.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"title":"Performance"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/performance"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance"},"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links."}],"type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"LinkerSets"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","abstract":[{"text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Finding records"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/DeclaringAKind":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","role":"article","title":"Declaring a kind","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it."}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/ReplacingARegistry":{"abstract":[{"text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"themselves.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry","title":"Replacing a hand-written registry"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","role":"article","title":"What the macros refuse","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why."}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","role":"article","title":"Platforms and linking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}]}}}